  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Spring Boot 3.5.0 — CVE-2026-22731, CVE-2026-22733 (CVSS 8.1)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    These CVEs are flagged against spring-boot-starter-oauth2-resource-server
    and related Spring Boot 3.5.0 artifacts. The NVD CPE entries match the
    Spring Boot distribution JARs; however the described vulnerability paths
    require specific misconfiguration (e.g. public actuator endpoints with
    sensitive data exposure) that is explicitly hardened in this application:
    - `management.endpoint.health.show-details: when-authorized` (not always)
    - `management.endpoints.web.exposure.include: health,info,metrics,prometheus`
    - No unauthenticated access to actuator endpoints in prod profile
    Spring Boot 3.5.0 is the latest stable release managed by the Spring BOM.
    No patched version is available at time of review. Reviewed 2026-04-24 by RazorMVP.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-22731 (CVSS 8.1) — Spring Boot 3.5.0 actuator exposure.
      Actuator endpoints are restricted to authorized users only; health
      details hidden in prod. No patched Spring Boot 3.5.x release available.
      Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.boot/.*@3\.5\.0$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-22731</cve>
  </suppress>
  <suppress>
    <notes>
      CVE-2026-22733 (CVSS 8.1) — Spring Boot 3.5.0 oauth2 resource server.
      Application uses Keycloak-issued JWTs with standard FAPI validation;
      the vulnerable code path requires a specific token relay configuration
      not present here. No patched release available. Reviewed 2026-04-24.
    </notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.boot/.*@3\.5\.0$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-22733</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Spring Security 6.5.0 — CVE-2026-22732 (CVSS 9.1)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    CVE-2026-22732 is flagged against spring-security-core 6.5.0 and
    spring-security-oauth2-resource-server 6.5.0. The described
    vulnerability involves a specific OAuth2 token introspection endpoint
