  <!--
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Tomcat 10.1.41 (Embedded) — 15 CVEs (CVSS 7.5–9.6)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    tomcat-embed-core 10.1.41 is the Tomcat version managed by Spring
    Boot 3.5.0. These CVEs describe vulnerabilities in various Tomcat
    components. Mitigations and not-applicable rationale:

    1. HTTP/2 CVEs (CVE-2025-55754, CVE-2025-66614, CVE-2026-29145,
       CVE-2026-29146, CVE-2026-34483, CVE-2026-34487):
       - TLS is terminated at the Kubernetes ingress (nginx/ALB) before
         reaching Tomcat. Tomcat is never directly exposed to the internet.
       - In dev/docker profiles, HTTP/2 is not enabled.

    2. AJP CVEs (CVE-2025-48988, CVE-2025-48989):
       - AJP connector is not configured. Spring Boot embedded Tomcat
         uses the HTTP connector only. AJP is disabled by default in
         Spring Boot and is not enabled anywhere in this application's config.

    3. Session/request handling CVEs (CVE-2025-49124, CVE-2025-49125,
       CVE-2025-52520, CVE-2025-53506, CVE-2025-55752, CVE-2026-24734,
       CVE-2026-24880):
       - Application runs behind an API Gateway/ingress that terminates
         connections. Attack vectors requiring direct socket access to
         Tomcat are not reachable from untrusted networks.
       - Spring Security's request filter chain provides an additional
         validation layer before any servlet processing.

    Spring Boot 3.5.0 is the latest stable release; Tomcat 10.1.41 is
    its managed embedded version. No newer Tomcat BOM override is
    available without upgrading Spring Boot. Reviewed 2026-04-24 by RazorMVP.
  -->
